### Phase 4 — Screen File Audit & Splitting

**Rule:** No screen file > 200 lines. No file mixes UI with business logic.

For each oversized screen, split into:

```
screen_name_page.dart          # Main page widget (<100 lines)
screen_name_body.dart          # Body content
screen_name_widgets.dart       # Sub-widgets private to this screen
```

**Files to split (identified as likely >200 lines):**

- [students_list_view.dart](file:///c:/Users/ENG%20AHMAD/Documents/GitHub/edufusion/lib/presentation/screens/students/students_list_view.dart) (243 lines) → split body out ✅ Priority
- `create_student_form.dart` — likely large, audit needed
- `exam_management.dart` — likely large, audit needed
- `general_settings_crestwood_academy.dart` — likely large
- `timetable_create_weekly_schedule.dart` — likely large
- Any BLoC file mixing events + states

---

### Phase 5 — BLoC Cleanup

**Rule:** Each BLoC gets **3 files**:
- `module_event.dart` — all events
- `module_state.dart` — all states  
- `module_bloc.dart` — the Bloc class itself

**Rule:** Every BLoC error state is handled. No `late` assignments that can throw.

**Pattern for safe error handling:**

```dart
// WRONG — crashes on network failure
emit(StudentsLoaded(students: data!));

// RIGHT — always handles null
if (data == null) {
  emit(StudentError('Failed to load students'));
  return;
}
emit(StudentsLoaded(students: data));
```

